---
source: misc/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"logger\")"
---
Enter messages into the system log

Usage: logger [OPTIONS] [MESSAGE]...

Arguments:
  [MESSAGE]...  Message to log

Options:
  -i                         Log the PID of the logger process
  -f, --file <FILE>          Log the contents of the specified file
  -e, --skip-empty           Skip empty lines when processing files
  -p, --priority <PRIORITY>  Set priority as facility.level or numeric (default: user.notice)
                             [default: user.notice]
  -s, --stderr               Also output message to stderr
  -t, --tag <TAG>            Tag every line with this tag (default: username)
  -u, --socket <SOCKET>      Write to the specified Unix socket instead of /dev/log
  -h, --help                 Print help
